    "explanationEn": "🎯 Why (B - 'Sum from t=1 to T of |P|^t') is the correct choice:\nA complete table must map every possible percept sequence of length 1 to T, requiring the summation of |P|^t for all t from 1 to T.\n\n💡 Real-World Example & Application:\nEvery added second exponentially multiplies rows; storing all possible 1-minute video sequences creates an astronomically huge table.\n\n❌ Why other options are incorrect:\n• (A - |P| * T): |P| * T assumes linear scaling, ignoring the fact that each successive time step multiplies previous sequences by |P|.\n• (C - T^|P|): T^|P| reverses base and exponent; the percept set size |P| is the branching base raised to power t.\n• (D - |P|!): |P|! represents permutations of percepts, which does not model sequences over time.",
    "questionAr": "إذا كان الوكيل يعمل لمدى الحياة بخطوات زمنية T مع مجموعة من التصورات المحتملة |P|، فكم عدد الإدخالات الإجمالية التي سيحتويها جدول البحث الكامل؟",
