    "explanationEn": "🎯 Why (B - 'Playing chess with a running game clock') is the correct choice:\nChess played with a clock is semidynamic: the board state remains static while you think, but the passage of time consumes your clock allocation.\n\n💡 Real-World Example & Application:\nApplications like robotic vacuums or smart climate control apply this principle to adapt to environmental changes and select rational actions.\n\n❌ Why other options are incorrect:\n• (A - Driving an automated taxi through urban traffic): Automated taxi driving is fully dynamic because surrounding vehicles and pedestrians move during planning.\n• (C - Solving a standard crossword puzzle): Standard crossword puzzles are completely static; neither grid contents nor scores degrade while pausing.\n• (D - Sorting parts on a moving conveyor belt): Sorting parts on a moving conveyor belt is dynamic because parts slide away if deliberation lags.",
