    "explanationEn": "🎯 Why (B - 'Yes; in solitaire card games the rules are known, but face-down cards cannot be seen') is the correct choice:\nYes; solitaire is a known environment because the rules are fully understood, but partially observable because cards in the deck face downward and are unseen.\n\n💡 Real-World Example & Application:\nDriving is continuous; vehicle velocity, steering angles, and trajectories evolve across smooth continuous real numbers.\n\n❌ Why other options are incorrect:\n• (A - No, knowing the rules guarantees full observability): Knowing physical laws or game rules does not grant sensory vision into face-down cards or occluded obstacles.\n• (C - Yes; in crossword puzzles the grid is partially invisible): Crossword puzzle grids are entirely visible to the solver at all times, making them fully observable.\n• (D - No, partial observability only occurs in unknown video games): Partial observability is ubiquitous in real-world scenarios and classic games with known rules like poker and solitaire.",
