    "explanationEn": "🎯 Why (A - 'The number of transistors on an integrated circuit doubles approximately every 18 to 24 months') is the correct choice:\nMoore's Law is the empirical observation that the number of transistors on microchips doubles roughly every 18 to 24 months.\n\n💡 Real-World Example & Application:\nModern intelligent systems like diagnostic medical engines and conversational agents rely on these historical foundations for rational decision-making.\n\n❌ Why other options are incorrect:\n• (B - Software error rates increase by 50% every year): Software defect rates depend on testing rigor, not an empirical semiconductor hardware doubling law.\n• (C - AI systems will replace all human workers by 1980): Predicting total human worker displacement by 1980 was hyperbole, not Moore's law.\n• (D - Computer screen resolutions double every week): Display resolution increases with panel manufacturing advances, not microchip transistor counts.",
